  "assumptions": [
    "Simplified simulation: no air resistance, ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down; horizontal speed stays constant and only vertical speed changes.",
    "Positions come exactly from the projectile formulas, so landing distance = speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8. The ball is a point (drawn 1 m in radius) and the flight ends when it returns to ground height.",
    "A hit is a landing within 1.5 m of the target centre, both edges counted; the red zone is exactly that 3 m wide. Targets come in a fixed order, so Reset starts the same challenge and clears score and trails.",
    "Each flight is shown over about two seconds, so screen time does not match the flight-time readout. Real balls slowed by air land shorter; 45° is best only without air resistance. Longest shot is about 64 m."
  ],
